    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s92",
     "source": "Remarks .—The Finnish h is pronounced as a guttural; nearly as Ger. ch in ich ."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s93",
     "source": "This is represented by ch in the above list."
    },
    {
     "id": "p001.s94",
     "source": "Every vowel should be pronounced by itself—not run together so as to make a totally different resultant sound, e.g. Aino should be pronounced not ī-nō , but ā´-ee-nō , the ā and ee being close together, with the greatest stress upon the ā , etc. i corresponds to English y in year ."
    }
